diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 6421c05..5e4aa46 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -56,6 +56,21 @@ synth = cyclosynth.Synthesizer(epsilon=1e-5, sqrt_t=True)
 r = synth.synthesize_u3(1.0472, 2.7577, 5.3947)
 ```
 
+For constructions requiring even T-count, use the Clifford+T search constraint:
+
+```python
+synth = cyclosynth.Synthesizer(epsilon=1e-8, even_t=True)
+r = synth.synthesize_u3(1.0472, 2.7577, 5.3947)
+if r:
+    assert r.t_count % 2 == 0
+```
+
+The constraint applies during candidate search and to shallow/diagonal fast
+paths. It keeps the same error tolerance and may increase the returned T-count
+or return `None` if no even candidate is found within the search bounds.
+The default is `even_t=False`; `even_t=True` with `sqrt_t=True` raises `ValueError`.
+Rust callers use `Synthesizer::new(epsilon, false).with_even_t(true)`.
+
 The `Synthesizer` constructor also exposes tuning knobs (`deadline_ms`, `q_cost`, …) for trading a little circuit cost for speed at deep ε; the defaults already minimize cost as far as my testing[...]
 
 Runnable demos are in [`examples/`](examples/).
